desktop = component "Desktop shell" {
metadata {
 harness_id "4677d33a-a6e5-4331-8e52-1a42de40beab"
 brief "Electron lifecycle; sandboxed renderer window and worker-backed runtime composition. Development Electron waits for the Vite renderer module. The developer-only CSP and explicit loopback proxy preserve renderer mount and desktop authentication."
 source "fact"
 status "verified"
 evidence "b4e0c245-401d-4f68-9009-f3ead2f2c98a d2142823-a131-422f-8961-c124d4f5df24 9f582baf-2f7a-41b6-9f88-875989fcc447"
 version "3"
}
}
renderer = component "Web renderer" {
metadata {
 harness_id "2d1c904d-2d74-4f20-9d7b-e4675d617cdf"
 brief "React views use shared DTOs and HTTP. Goal title full-text previews stay anchored to the title across hover, focus and click, preserving selectable scrolling and viewport clamping. User message bubbles fit their content, stay right-aligned and wrap within responsive maximum widths. Reply copy controls center both copy and success glyphs within explicit button dimensions. Each turn projects only its last thinking phase into stable tool disclosures; expanding reveals a bounded public summary while complete execution history stays intact. The accessible extension list uses a distinct puzzle glyph and shows names and fixed-size switches for Subagents, local Agent Browser and Safety Net, without helper copy. Missing private history remains an internal marker without explanatory UI text. Drafts restore current selections; removed cloud IDs do not enable the replacement. Native partners omit Pi extensions and settings stays last. Partner tool cards use one default-off Agent Browser switch to select or clear the complete browser family while retaining independent core choices. Complete saved selections restore as on; legacy partial selections save as off without widening. Counts treat the family once, catalog failures preserve permissions, and switch geometry supports keyboard input, themes and narrow layouts. History actions offer title editing with selected input, keyboard save/cancel, pending guards and retry; saved titles update history, search and the selected header without resetting drafts. Safe current-turn SSE updates preserve loaded history, drafts and titles; generation counters reject stale refreshes, and disconnected streams fall back to 100 ms cursors. Scoped reads have timeout, cancellation, backoff and selection epochs. Successful reads and accepted stream snapshots clear only their connection notice; authentication rejection stops automatic reads and closes the stream. Model recovery and safe execution failures remain distinct. Model forms share expanded 2M/3M context and 256K/300K/512K output tiers. New connections select 1M/128K; existing recommended and custom limits survive editing. LAN browsers share conversation UI through authenticated HTTP without local workspace controls. Responsive history closes on narrow transitions. The legacy paired fallback reuses conversation and archive views through a restricted command adapter. Routine continuation editing retains its controlled goal id while pending, running or blocked runs lock target selection. Evolution settings display independent source groups, reproduction and comparison counts, pause causes and retry times, and distinguish sample waits from explicit pauses. Goal cards distinguish queued synthesis and scheduled retry from active summarization, showing persisted attempts and retry time; paired browser badges consume the same optional projection. Message composers share Enter submission, Shift+Enter line breaks and IME confirmation. Active tool, turn and stop states animate with a static reduced-motion treatment. Completed turns show one footer status and only disclose context inside existing activity details. Read-only partner transcripts share ordinary chat Markdown and compact paired tool groups. Partner transcript prose uses the ordinary 13px base, with 12px dispatched task bubbles. Goal and workbench views retain their own history, artifact and authorized local trace actions. Ordinary chat history, workbenches and the remembered transcript load independently of configuration. Session-scoped list summaries render on return and stale results cannot undo changes. Partner transcript first and earlier pages skip card aggregation, while active refresh updates status. Completed replies offer compact copy and fork actions on desktop and LAN web. Opening a fork carries the selected configuration into an empty composer. Sidebar workbench groups and their conversation rows use browser-profile drag and keyboard ordering, preserving conversation ownership and keeping local preference writes inside the renderer. Inline question cards preserve conversation/goal history and keep draft state scoped by question identity and version. Ordinary chat uses compact forms and default-collapsed one-line question and answer receipts. Goal feeds show compact active and queued forms. Goal detail and result views place resolved cards behind a question history disclosure; the legacy paired task card uses the same collapsed disclosure. ACTIVE cards show server deadlines and recommendations; queued cards stay read-only, and receipts distinguish answer source from delivery. Explicit interrupted recovery distinguishes saved answers from choosing the displayed default. Question arrival anchors the card heading instead of scrolling past it; paired answers require questions.v1. Agent panels page results by stable cursors with one in-flight refresh and retain successful pages across errors. Goal detail polls a summary and refreshes visible map pages only when their version changes. Goal details request at most 100 recent Agent cards and keep their transcript selection goal-scoped."
 source "fact"
 status "verified"
 evidence "bb0959ec-71ad-48ea-824b-3aa91a15a7a1 b4fa28c9-1351-4ac0-aa75-af6c6f4e48a9 2bee49b0-f04c-4ce2-8f64-79516009c1e9 e5ed42e2-c606-4dd6-8d01-a16986fe9ba0 4533c5a3-4aba-4fcb-bc4c-7c1f7d7d5c30 bdb1be5c-c983-4e99-8b95-e1f0df5ed37f 08e91490-c42a-42e1-a0c5-4a40c1e2fe0e e5438320-e3e9-41e2-abf9-b409867822e0 ececa617-c6a3-4ea1-a324-a7feb9d2e600 8dc57d83-a63f-4aaf-9cec-21a2a3252c29 f1700bac-e723-4de3-b839-f99c567e6d08 6097810a-ce3d-4038-9a5c-f30fc8382210 c3ae40e3-2672-4b92-b011-b2ef3c6044a8 5bc37929-aa0f-458c-98ae-57aa0ea8090e 2a3aff22-8581-424c-af0a-c4182b77742f 8b99a8d3-c9b5-4f56-aca5-67d33579c709 9b9178f5-d29c-46e3-be65-8f7760ea0055 c4daa482-036e-467b-849b-5c3041e5d812 a8d58319-cdbe-4c6d-ab62-1d334fa3b766 924fa695-204b-44c7-a782-358227365952 bf6ad363-5fc0-4a19-9332-de2c603b9e8c 85794627-0653-4404-bc02-7c4deb5225cd cea47700-6070-440d-8bb0-71bb202849a8 18da4429-806e-4b16-b3d4-1363a15b85aa 68e4f10a-361b-41e7-b7cd-8e3d97365210 3627078a-b447-432c-9b65-37a1521deadb 19825361-c0da-4b03-b1bb-abfe0bef46ed 0d39bd91-cffc-4674-a1da-a6e3c7d8393e a2186992-b051-47e8-bdce-a4e4d8878e40 c08040c4-15d6-410b-b52d-ca49f3aca31f bf81ead4-46f4-40a9-9739-6f928dc67c99 7c9cf77f-e85f-499b-b696-3ea0feb3e744 515cd0c5-32bb-48ab-a20c-7980095c1387 250b18ae-151c-4f63-89a2-c782e29fcd65 9771fb1a-d3da-408f-b0ad-e65befa20813 7ec7db0b-af8f-4977-864c-3c7a8a598f96 18211c85-8a28-4f54-95f6-1c0590170f91 9181c052-4571-46ae-886a-db3112665f2f 7feb1381-875f-4ecb-aae3-775f884080f3 7cbf32eb-15bd-4f20-91e1-84e61b5cbe6a fce68d9c-8f3e-46a1-a6c6-f1d4705e36ac ff21dcb3-2e6a-441d-b7e9-956c4678f044 5cc8dd07-5b08-4c9e-a9da-fc71b178abaa 88a9fe42-acd0-477e-bfe8-c4b56d0485bf 84fb4077-4a9e-444a-8c06-146bdeaff8c4"
 version "39"
}
}
