validation = component "Quality gates" {
metadata {
 harness_id "cfebb4bc-4ef2-4661-bd04-0d17d7f6619f"
 brief "Boundary scanner classifies allowed imports; npm scripts define checks and packaging. The Node 24 Windows/macOS quality matrix requires a complete shared lock graph, including optional WASM peer dependencies, before builds and tests. Read-only planning compares numeric stable package and Latest versions before the matrix. Only eligible main push/manual version upgrades build native Windows NSIS or macOS DMG installers and upload separate 14-day artifacts after quality gates; missing installers fail. Same/older versions, PRs and other refs retain all quality gates while skipping installers and publication. The serialized publisher rechecks Latest and generates nonempty version notes from the prior Latest tag to the current commit before creating or publishing a draft; existing releases remain immutable. Push, pull-request and manual triggers share the pipeline. Package commands rebuild production, audit contents and explicitly disable electron-builder publication, so CI packaging needs no GitHub Release token; a separate serialized main-only job downloads both installers from the same successful matrix run and publishes package-version tags with EXE, DMG and SHA-256 checksums. Only this job has contents-write through the automatic token. Uploads stay in draft until all assets are confirmed; published versions are preserved and interrupted drafts require the original commit; signing certificates and notarization remain outside this CI flow. Isolated npm 11.19.1 lock validation supplements installed-tree checks. Two real-disk persistence scenarios have explicit bounded CI wait budgets; local budgets, transaction counts, privacy assertions and coverage gates remain enforced. Streaming regressions cover synthetic Pi callbacks, committed projections, transport cleanup, short-answer display, stale reads and an isolated Electron event stream. Renderer and disposable Electron checks verify model creation defaults, expanded limit submissions and retained saved values. Cross-platform conversation regressions cover command admission, device-scoped paging, restricted browser adapters, no-preload viewport behavior and encrypted/native widget paths. Disposable lease regressions cover waiting projections, same-identity resume and completion, canceled cards and bounded Git inspection without external commands. Local checks follow the change-scope matrix, with targeted regressions and static checks first; Electron/native verification, coverage and builds require relevant boundaries or explicit full/release scope. Passing checks and current artifacts are reused. Scoped model-call regressions enforce configured output maxima, preserve provider/context constraints and distinguish structural preflight from quality evaluation. Anthropic auth retries preserve configured output limits and the same no-tool request across credential modes. Fixture-inclusive Windows CI case deadlines are 30 seconds; other CI platforms retain 15 seconds and local defaults retain 5 seconds. The 100,000-row activity scenario keeps its one-second query assertion; worker limits, business assertions and coverage gates remain enforced. The Electron development smoke test completes disposable setup through the Vite proxy and opens ordinary conversations. Android packaging uses the root project version for the APK manifest and filename, and the Flutter build code for device upgrades. HIST regressions cover provider request admission, migration, Work isolation and private evidence reuse with fake models and disposable stores. Disposable coverage regressions exercise conflict scope, receipt failure classes, restart projection and Unicode context limits. ASK-01-12 records scoped FIFO/CAS, atomic goal pauses, canonical Pi acknowledgement, cursor/recovery and cross-platform question acceptance seams. Synthetic SDK/HTTP and widget coverage does not establish real-provider quality, physical Android devices or public-network behavior. The project verify recipe drives a disposable real Electron/HTTP/SQLite/SDK flow with a local synthetic Responses model, original-call observation, edge probes and inspected screenshots; it is a procedure, not a durable run receipt. A disposable large-goal WAL scenario checks two clients against concurrent status writes, complete paging and HTTP latency budgets. Incremental knowledge regressions deny reads of old result bodies and newly sealed source text. Disposable Routine tests verify admission-time sequence reuse; goal Agent tests exercise the bounded card and transcript window."
